                <pb facs="1117" n="1037" xml:id="pg1037"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Leishman to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-07-11"><hi rendition="#italic">July 11,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Replying to Department’s telegram of July 9, Mr. Leishman reports that the
                    matter referred to had already received his attention and that a demand has been
                    made for the surrender of the package; that he will continue to use good offices
                    in behalf of the company, and that the origin of the trouble is fully explained
                    in his dispatches Nos. 210 and 218.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
